@startuml
' Evidence: Laplace/app/Laplace.Endpoints.OpenAICompat/Auth/ApiKeys.cs SHA256 0a0f460b4fb97cb84442b0e9fbc96d961691e292f910d6d729bbce2c37647081
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFCFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
title Monorepo — API-key issue, validation, touch and revocation
start
if (Issue?) then (yes)
 :Generate 24 random bytes; lowercase hex with sk-laplace- prefix;
 :SHA256 full key; store hash, 16-character display prefix, tenant and label;
 :Await store write; return plaintext key and record;
elseif (Validate?) then (yes)
 :Require prefix; hash full presented key; query store;
 if (Missing or revoked?) then (yes)
  :Return no identity;
 else (active)
  :Write LastUsedAt; return previously read record;
 endif
elseif (Revoke by prefix?) then (yes)
 :Read tenant keys; choose first active exact-prefix match;
 :Revoke selected key hash or return false;
else (list)
 :Read keys by tenant or exact label;
endif
stop
footer
Source-reviewed orchestration. Nested semantics remain open; no runtime acceptance
claimed. Complete key service and both stores reviewed. Validation performs a read then
separate usage write; revocation is not transactionally rechecked before returning the
previously read record. In-memory touch/revoke use dictionary read/replace operations and
do not provide an atomic compare-update across both. PostgreSQL issue uses ON CONFLICT DO
NOTHING; tenant foreign-key violation has a specific error. Plaintext is returned by
issuance, not stored by these stores.
end footer

@enduml
